      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 34,
      "line_end": 35,
      "title": "Search query built from request input",
      "description": "Search formats the name query parameter directly into the SQL text with Sprintf. A quote in name escapes the string literal. Any client calling GET /users can read or change arbitrary database rows. Use a placeholder in the query and pass name to QueryContext as a bound argument.",
      "suggested_change": "rows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search formats the name query parameter directly into the SQL text with Sprintf. A quote in name escapes the string literal.",
      "consequence": "Any client calling GET /users can read or change arbitrary database rows.",
      "fix": "Use a placeholder in the query and pass name to QueryContext as a bound argument."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 63,
      "line_end": 63,
      "title": "Mutex left locked on missing key",
      "description": "Count locks h.mu and then returns early when key is empty without unlocking. The mutex stays held forever. One request to GET /count without a key blocks every later Count request permanently. Check key before taking the lock, or defer h.mu.Unlock() right after locking.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Count locks h.mu and then returns early when key is empty without unlocking. The mutex stays held forever.",
      "consequence": "One request to GET /count without a key blocks every later Count request permanently.",
      "fix": "Check key before taking the lock, or defer h.mu.Unlock() right after locking."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 83,
      "line_end": 83,
      "title": "Response body closed before error check",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close() before checking err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil and the deferred call dereferences it. An unreachable upstream makes GET /upstream panic instead of returning 502. Move the defer after the err check.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close() before checking err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil and the deferred call dereferences it.",
      "consequence": "An unreachable upstream makes GET /upstream panic instead of returning 502.",
      "fix": "Move the defer after the err check."
    },
